<div class="bg-amber-50 border-l-4 border-amber-500 p-4 my-4"><p class="font-semibold mb-1">Quick Answer: How much does folded leaflet printing cost?</p><p class="text-sm">Folded leaflets run <strong>HK$0.70-1.95 per leaflet</strong> from <strong>10 pieces</strong>.<br/>Why more than a flat flyer? For the same A4 press sheet, flat flyers (FL-001 / FL-003) are <strong>HK$0.35-0.95 per piece</strong> while folded leaflets are <strong>HK$0.70-1.95</strong> — the difference is <strong>creasing, folding labour and the heavier 157gsm / 200gsm art paper</strong>. Check live pricing on the <a href="/product/folded-leaflets/">Folded Leaflets FL-004</a> product page with a 30-second AI quote.</p></div>

<div class="bg-amber-50 border-l-4 border-amber-500 p-4 my-4"><p class="font-semibold mb-1">Quick Answer: What is the minimum order for folded leaflets?</p><p class="text-sm">Just <strong>10 pieces</strong> — there is no 500-piece minimum, so you can test a campaign before committing to bulk. Unit price drops on the same ladder as the rest of the range: <strong>100 pieces at list price, 500 at 20% off, 1,000 at 35% off, 5,000 at 50% off</strong>. Folded leaflets sit inside the <a href="/en/category/flyers/">flyer printing category</a>, where A4 and A5 flyers, thick paper flyers and same-day flyers also start at 10 pieces and can be combined into one order.</p></div>

<div class="bg-amber-50 border-l-4 border-amber-500 p-4 my-4"><p class="font-semibold mb-1">Quick Answer: Bi-fold, tri-fold or Z-fold?</p><p class="text-sm"><strong>Bi-fold</strong> (A4 flat becomes A5 finished, 148×210mm) is the cheapest and gives the largest panels for a single message. <strong>Tri-fold letter fold</strong> (A4 flat becomes DL finished, 99×210mm) is the standard handout format and <strong>drops straight into a DL envelope</strong> for mailing. <strong>Z-fold</strong> opens out to six equal panels, ideal for processes, course schedules and price ladders. <strong>Gate fold</strong> opens to the largest spread for maps, guides and event graphics. See the comparison table below.</p></div>

