<h2>4. Artwork specs: bleed, safety margin and fold positions</h2>
<p>The one thing that separates folded artwork from flat artwork is that <strong>the crease lines cut the sheet into separate panels</strong>, and each panel has to be designed as its own layout.</p>
<ol>
  <li><strong>3mm bleed</strong> on all four edges; backgrounds and photos must extend to the bleed line so nothing shows white after trimming.</li>
  <li><strong>5mm safety margin:</strong> keep text and logos at least 5mm inside the trim line to absorb cutting tolerance.</li>
  <li><strong>1-2mm clearance at creases:</strong> the crease line is a high-wear area — never place key copy, barcodes or logos across it.</li>
  <li><strong>Narrow the inner panel</strong> by 1-2mm on tri-folds and heavier stocks so the finished leaflet closes flat.</li>
  <li><strong>Colour:</strong> supply CMYK; set black text as single black (K100) to avoid four-colour ghosting; images at 300dpi.</li>
  <li><strong>Mark the folds</strong> on a separate spot-colour layer for the printer, and keep them off the final printed layer.</li>
</ol>
<p>For a general pre-flight checklist, read the <a href="/en/blog/flyer-printing-guide/">complete flyer printing guide</a>. Food and beverage readers should also see the <a href="/en/blog/menu-buying-guide/">menu printing buying guide</a> and the <a href="/product/pvc-menus/">PVC menus product page</a> for menu and leaflet combinations.</p>

<h2>5. Frequently asked questions</h2>
<p><strong>Q1: What is the smallest quantity of folded leaflets I can order?</strong><br/><strong>10 pieces.</strong> Runs of 10-100 go through digital printing, which suits test drops and internal sign-off; above 1,000 pieces offset printing is substantially cheaper per piece.</p>
<p><strong>Q2: Should I print folded leaflets or flat flyers?</strong><br/>One message, one offer → a flat flyer (<a href="/product/a4-flyers/">from HK$0.35 per piece</a>). Layered information — brand story, products, price list and store addresses — or a piece that must fit a DL envelope → folded leaflets (<a href="/product/folded-leaflets/">from HK$0.70 per piece</a>). The premium buys six usable panels and a stiffer, more considered feel.</p>
<p><strong>Q3: 157gsm or 200gsm art paper?</strong><br/>157gsm is the standard choice, balancing stiffness against a clean fold, and is best for street distribution. 200gsm feels more substantial and suits brand packs and premium menus, but demands tighter scoring and folding — pair it with lamination.</p>
<p><strong>Q4: How long does production take, and can you rush it?</strong><br/>Standard turnaround is <strong>3-5 working days</strong>. Same-day delivery is available on digital rush jobs; allow five working days or more for offset runs above 1,000 pieces. Tell us the distribution date when you order.</p>
<p><strong>Q5: Can I print different content per version, such as different store addresses?</strong><br/>Yes. Variable data printing (VDP) can change text, addresses or numbering within a single run, which suits chains and tiered membership programmes — just supply the version list alongside the quantity.</p>

